static.solution:
\vec{OP}=\left\lt 0,7,6\right> and \vec{OQ}=\left\lt 0,7,4\right>. Thus,



S=\frac{1}{2} || \vec{OP} \times \vec{OQ} ||



We compute the cross product:



\vec{OP} \times \vec{OQ}=
\left| \begin{array}{ccc}
 \boldsymbol{i} \amp  \boldsymbol{j} \amp  \boldsymbol{k} \\
 0 \amp  7 \amp  6 \\
 0 \amp  7 \amp  4
\end{array} \right|
= 
  \left| \begin{array}{cc} 7 \amp  6 \\ 7 \amp  4 \end{array} \right| \boldsymbol{i}
- \left| \begin{array}{cc} 0 \amp  6 \\ 0 \amp  4 \end{array} \right| \boldsymbol{j}
+ \left| \begin{array}{cc} 0 \amp  7 \\ 0 \amp  7 \end{array} \right| \boldsymbol{k} 


\qquad = -14 \boldsymbol{i} + 0 \boldsymbol{j} + 0 \boldsymbol{k}



S=\frac{1}{2}|| -14 \boldsymbol{i} + 0 \boldsymbol{j} + 0 \boldsymbol{k} ||
   =\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{(-14)^2+(0)^2+(0)^2}
   \approx 7.
